# Autism Brain Imaging Data Exchange II (ABIDE-II)

ABIDE II is the second initiative of the Autism Brain Imaging Data Exchange
(ABIDE), an effort of the International Neuroimaging Data-sharing
Initiative (INDI). Its 19 sites, among which institutions that contributed
to ABIDE I and new members, share resting state functional magnetic
resonance imaging (R-fMRI), anatomical and phenotypic datasets of
individuals with Autism Spectrum Disorder (ASD) and of typical controls.
Some sites also share diffusion imaging data, and two sites share
longitudinal data (a second session of individuals scanned earlier).

In accordance with HIPAA guidelines and 1000 Functional Connectomes Project /
INDI protocols, all datasets have been anonymized, with no protected health
information included.

Data usage agreement, credits and acknowledgements:
https://fcon_1000.projects.nitrc.org/indi/abide/abide_II.html

## This dataset

Converted to BIDS by brainspresso (`bx abide2`) from the NITRC release
(`ABIDEII-<SITE>_<sample>.tar.gz` images, `ABIDEII-<SITE>_<sample>.csv`
phenotypes). Sidecars are built from the protocol printouts of each site
and sample, not from the DICOM headers.
